ee.cu:16]\n          │           │\n          │           └─ bn254_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes() [Rust wrapper, /home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/bn254_merkle_tree.rs:245]\n          │               └─> _bn254_poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes [FFI, bn254_poseidon2.cu:425]\n          │                   └─> bn254_compressing_row_hashes_kernel [bn254_poseidon2.cu:183]\n          │\n          └─ Loop: While digest_layers.last().len() > 1\n              └─> compress_layer() per layer [/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs:152]\n                  └─> GpuMerkleHash::compress_layer()\n                      └─> poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer() [Rust wrapper, cuda/merkle_tree.rs:132]\n                          └─> _poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer [FFI, merkle_tree.cu:267]\n                              └─> poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel [merkle_tree.cu:153] (with stride=1)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. POSEIDON2 HASHING: SINGLE-STREAM OR MULTI-STREAM\n\n**Answer: ALL SINGLE STREAM (default CUDA stream 0)**\n\nEvidence:\n- No explicit stream creation in any Rust wrapper code\n- No `cudaStreamCreate`, `cudaStreamDestroy`, or stream parameters in FFI declarations\n- All kernel launches use default launch syntax `kernel<<<grid, block>>>` which uses stream 0\n- No async memory copies or explicit synchronization between stacked operations\n- MemTracker metrics suggest synchronous execution with implicit device sync at function boundaries\n\nThis means **all kernels in a trace commit are sequentially dependent on the same stream**, which limits parallelization opportunities.\n\n---\n\n### 3. KERNEL LAUNCHES PER SEGMENT\n\nFor a complete trace commit with height = query_stride × 2^log_rows_per_query:\n\n**Fixed kernels (per segment):**\n1. `stack_columns_kernel` - 1 launch\n   - Grid: `(num_descriptors, 1, 1)`, Block: `(256, 1, 1)`\n   - Scatters trace columns into expanded layout\n\n2. `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kern