size,\n) -> Result<(), CudaError>\n```\n\n### 6. CUDA KERNEL IMPLEMENTATIONS\n\n**Location**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/`\n\n#### 6a. Zerocheck Kernel (`zerocheck_round0.cu`, 731 lines)\n\n**Key components**:\n- `acc_constraints()` device function (lines 33-138) — evaluates DAG with lambda weighting\n- Two kernel implementations:\n  1. **NTT-based lockstep kernel** (lines 148-247): Each thread handles ALL cosets\n  2. **Coset-parallel kernel** (lines 250-467): grid.y = num_cosets, each block handles one coset\n- Selects mode based on threshold: `COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD = 32768` (2^15)\n- Uses encoded `Rule` type (u128) for compact DAG representation\n- Lazy rule decoding: only header (op, flags, x) decoded upfront\n- Shared memory layout:\n  - `FpExt[blockDim.x]` for reduction\n  - Optional `Fp[blockDim.x]` for NTT scratch buffers (NEEDS_SHMEM template)\n\n**Thread layout**:\n- `ntt_idx = threadIdx.x % skip_domain` (varies fastest)\n- `x_int = threadIdx.x >> l_skip`\n- Block size: `skip_domain * x_per_block` where `x_per_block` is computed based on temp buffer budget\n\n**Launch configuration** (lines 523-591):\n- Grid: depends on num_x, skip_domain, buffer_size, max_temp_bytes\n- Final reduction: `sumcheck::final_reduce_block_sums` kernel over NUM_COSETS × skip_domain grid\n\n#### 6b. Logup Kernel (`logup_round0.cu`, 812 lines)\n\n**Key components**:\n- `acc_interactions()` device function (lines 37-153) — evaluates DAG with numer/denom weighting\n- Two kernel implementations:\n  1. **NTT-based lockstep kernel**: Each thread handles ALL cosets, tracks both numer/denom sums\n  2. **Coset-parallel kernel**: grid.y = num_cosets, per-coset handling with identity-coset optimization\n- Same threshold strategy as zerocheck: `COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD = 32768`\n- Uses `FracExt` output type (numerator/denominator fractions)\n- Handles `FIRST_COSET_IS_IDENTITY` optimization to skip iNTT for coset 0\n\n### 7. DATA STRUCTURES\n\n**Round0AirResult** (lines 114-119):\n```rust\nstruct Round0AirResult {\n    trace_idx: usize,\n    zerocheck_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,\n    logup_numer_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,\n    logup_denom_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,\n}\n```\n\n**LogupZerocheckGpu struct** (lines 576-637):\n```rust\npub struct LogupZerocheckGpu<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n    // Precomputed lambdas and challenges\n    pub lambda_pows: Option<DeviceBuffer<EF>>,           // [max_num_constraints]\n    lambda_combinations: Vec<Option<DeviceBuffer<EF>>>,  // per-AIR, for monomial evaluation\n    pub d_challenges: DeviceBuffer<EF>,                  // [alpha, beta^0, ..., beta^max_len]\n    \n    // Per-trace metadata\n    n_per_trace: Vec<isize>,                             // log2 height per trace\n    public_values_per_trace: Vec<DeviceBuffer<F>>,       // per-trace public values\n    eq_3b_per_trace: Vec<Vec<EF>>,                        // eq_3b weights (CPU)\n    d_eq_3b_per_trace: Vec<DeviceBuffer<EF>>,            // eq_3b weights (device)\n    sels_per_trace_base: Vec<DeviceMatrix<F>>,           // hypercube selectors\n    \n    // Memory management\n    memory_limit_bytes: usize,                           // total budget per segment\n    // ... other fields\n}\n```\n\n### 8. MULTI-THREADING CONFIGURATION\n\n**Lines 95, 939-943**:\n```rust\nconst NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS: usize = 8;  // Per-thread CUDA streams\n\nlet num_threads = if work_items.len() >= 100 {\n    NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())\n} else {\n    1\n};\n```\n\n**Key aspects**:\n- 8 OS threads each with per-thread CUDA stream (`cudaStreamPerThread`)\n- Threshold: only use multi-threading for ≥100 AIRs (avoids overhead for few large AIRs at APC 0)\n- Memory budget per thread: `per_thread_temp_bytes = memory_limit_bytes / NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS`\n- Work distribution: sorted by descending height, split into sequential chunks\n- Synchronization: `current_stream_sync()` barrier before spawning threads\n\n### 9. COMPLETE CALL CHAIN\n\n```\nsumcheck_uni_round0_polys() [217 lines]\n  ├─ Phase 1: Build work_items (CPU)\n  │   ├─ Precompute lambda_pows.to_device()\n  │   ├─ Compute lambda_combinations per AIR\n  │   ├─ Compute eq_3b_per_trace, d_eq_3b_per_trace\n  │   ├─ Compute eq_xis layers\n  │   └─ Build sels_per_trace_base\n  │\n  ├─ Phase 2a: Single-threaded path (work_items.len() < 100)\n  │   └─ For each work_item:\n  │       └─ process_air_round0(w) [133 lines]\n  │           ├─ main_parts.to_device() [H2D]\n  │           ├─ evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu() [rounds0.rs:31-124]\n  │           │   ├─ Alloc intermediates, temp_sums_buffer, sp_evals\n  │           │   └─ Launch zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints() [CUDA kernel]\n  │           │       └─ CPU D2H: sum_buffer.to_host_on_current_stream()\n  │           ├─ Transpose + iDFT + poly construction [CPU]\n  │           ├─ evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu() [rounds0.rs:132-276]\n  │           │   ├─ Build interaction DAG (CPU) each time\n  │           │   ├─ Alloc intermediates, temp_sums_buffer, s_evals\n  │           │   ├─ numer_weights.to_device() [H2D]\n  │           │   ├─ denom_weights.to_device() [H2D]\n  │           │   ├─ d_rules.to_device() [H2D]\n  │           │   └─ Launch logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0() [CUDA kernel]\n  │           │       └─ CPU D2H: sum.to_host_on_current_stream()\n  │           └─ Unpack + iDFT + poly construction [CPU]\n  │\n  ├─ Phase 2b: Multi-threaded path (work_items.len() >= 100)\n  │   ├─ std::thread::scope with 8 threads\n  │   │   └─ Each thread: for each AIR in chunk:\n  │   │       └─ process_air_round0(w) [same as 2a]\n  │   └─ Join all threads, collect results\n  │\n  └─ Phase 3: Scatter results (CPU)\n      └─ Collect polynomials into batch_sp_poly array\n```\n\n### 10. PERFORMANCE CHARACTERISTICS\n\n**Round 0 Performance at APC 300**:\n- **Baseline (without optimizations)**: 662ms\n- **Current (with 8-thread multi-stream)**: 301ms  \n- **Improvement**: 2.20x (361ms saved