tter results (CPU)\n      └─ Collect polynomials into batch_sp_poly array\n```\n\n### 10. PERFORMANCE CHARACTERISTICS\n\n**Round 0 Performance at APC 300**:\n- **Baseline (without optimizations)**: 662ms\n- **Current (with 8-thread multi-stream)**: 301ms  \n- **Improvement**: 2.20x (361ms saved)\n- **Bottleneck analysis** (from autoopt logs):\n  - 76% overhead (non-kernel time) in per-AIR path\n  - GPU kernel execution: ~70-80ms\n  - CPU post-processing (transpose, iDFT): ~50-70ms per segment\n  - Kernel launch overhead: ~1500 launches × ~15-20μs = 22.5-30ms\n  - Per-AIR buffer allocation/deallocation via VPMM pool\n\n**Current bottleneck**: Even with multi-threading, sequential per-AIR kernels cannot fully overlap. Attempted batching solution (consolidating AIRs into single kernel launch) was blocked by Rust optimizer interference.\n\n### 11. OPTIMIZER INTERFERENCE ISSUE\n\n**From `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays/report.md`**:\n\nThe attempted descriptor array batching optimization failed because:\n- Added orchestration code to `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` (router logic for small AIRs to batched path)\n- This caused `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` crashes at APC 300, even when batched code path never executed\n- Root cause: Rust LLVM optimizer changed code generation for the entire function, affecting the existing multi-threaded CUDA kernel launch path\n- Symptom: memory safety issues in unchanged code (multi-threaded H2D copies, kernel launches)\n- The 217-line function is apparently at a compiler optimization boundary\n\n**Unresolved**: Whether this is due to:\n1. Function size threshold for aggressive optimization passes\n2. Optimizer interaction with thread spawning code\n3. Register pressure changes affecting pointer/reference tracking\n4. Inlining of utility functions changing memory access patterns\n\n### 12. KEY OBSERVATIONS\n\n1. **No per-AIR descriptor batching exists currently** — each AIR gets its own kernel launch sequence:\n   - 1 zerocheck kernel + 1 logup kernel per AIR\n   - ~1500 total kernel launches per segment at APC 300\n\n2. **Interaction DAG reconstruction is per-AIR** (lines 161-207 of `round0.rs`):\n   - `SymbolicDagBuilder` instantiated fresh for each AIR\n   - ~310 DAG constructions per segment (not cached at keygen)\n   - CPU overhead: ~1-2ms per AIR\n\n3. **Memory budget distribution**:\n   - `memory_limit_bytes` = ~5GB (default or save_memory mode)\n   - Divided by 8 threads: ~625MB per thread for intermediates\n   - Could support larger batch sizes if batching were enabled\n\n4. **Stream synchronization**:\n   - Each worker thread uses `cudaStreamPerThread` (implicit per-OS-thread stream)\n   - No explicit synchronization between threads' GPU work — only final join\n   - Barrier before thread spawn: `current_stream_sync()` ensures prior uploads visible\n\n5. **Why multi-threading helps**:\n   - Enables concurrent kernel execution on different SMs\n   - Without it, kernels serialize on single stream\n   - Alleviates GPU underutilization when per-AIR kernels are small/medium sized\n\n6. **Optimization ceiling without batching**:\n   - ~301ms current at APC 300 with 8 threads\n   - Estimated max via batching: ~100-180ms (from nsys analysis showing 76% overhead)\n   - Batching would reduce kernel launch count from 1500 to ~30 (organized by num_cosets)\n   - But implementation blocked by compiler optimization side effects\n\n---\n\n**Files read**:\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (main entry, lines 95, 114-138, 140-272, 576-637, 767-983)\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs` (per-AIR evaluation, 275 lines)\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (FFI bindings, lines 311-332, 351-373, 962-1005, 1015-1058)\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu` (731 lines)\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu` (812 lines)\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays/report.md` (descriptor batching attempt analysis)\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/log.md` (optimization history)"}],"totalDurationMs":119156,"totalTokens":66112,"totalToolUseCount":34,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":59167,"output_tokens":6593,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":349},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":6593,"cache_read_input_tokens":59167,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":349,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":14,"searchCount":4,"bashCount":16,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
