f keeping the code paths separate. Instead, I should keep the existing `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` function as-is and add the new batched variant alongside it, letting the caller choose which path to take based on the workload characteristics.\n\nThe tricky part is that the existing function iterates over all AIRs in `self.pk.per_air`, so I'd need to either temporarily mask out small AIRs before calling it, or refactor the iteration logic to accept a filter. Looking at the function signature...\n\nExamining the function structure...\n\nActually, I think the cleanest path forward is to split `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` into three phases: building work items on the CPU, processing them with multi-streaming on the GPU, and scattering results back—then route large and small AIRs through different processing pipelines based on their size.\n\nThe key insight is that extracting Phase 2 into its own function is the only change to existing code, and marking it with `#[inline(never)]` prevents the optimizer from making cross-function optimizations that might trigger the bug, keeping each processing unit isolated.\n\nNow I'm checking my measurement targets—if Round 0 drops from 301ms to 100-150ms, that's a 150-200ms savings that should push STARK excl trace down to around 1229-1279ms, which would represent roughly a 2x improvement over the 2455ms baseline.\n\nFor scaling across different APC levels, I'm looking at a ratio of about 1.68-1.75x between APC 0 and APC 300, which is closer to the 2x target but still not quite there.\n\nBefore I formalize the plan, I want to explore whether there's a simpler path forward—what if I just doubled the multi-stream thread count for Round 0 from 8 to 16 threads instead, since the previous jump from 4 to 8 threads already yielded a 15ms improvement?\n\nGoing to 16 threads could potentially save another 45ms if there's still GPU headroom, which is straightforward to implement but modest compared to the 150-200ms gains from batching. I'll keep this as a backup option while prioritizing the batching approach, then move on to writing out the formal plan and getting it reviewed.\n\nNow I'm checking the previous batch-round0-descriptor-arrays task to see what was already attempted and what I can build on.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9211,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8341,"cache_read_input_tokens":69822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8341},"output_tokens":30,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d386d521-3ea3-445a-958b-d64302191775","uuid":"7d58d0e5-db09-462d-9591-7e240ab24225"}
