{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C4t8kw1RviKpxTUJKVhqit","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays\n2\t\n3\tReplace per-AIR Round 0 kernel launches with batched descriptor-array kernels for both zerocheck constraint evaluation and logup interaction evaluation. Currently, each of the ~310 AIRs per segment at APC 300 gets 2+ individual kernel launches, buffer allocations, and H2D copies, resulting in ~1500 kernel launches per segment — nsys profiling shows 76% of Round 0 wall time (294ms) is overhead, not GPU compute. By caching the interaction DAG structure at keygen and batching all per-AIR contexts into a single H2D upload + single kernel launch (using the proven descriptor-array pattern from MLE batch kernels), we expect to reduce Round 0 from 294ms to ~100ms at APC 300, saving ~190ms from STARK excl trace.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d386d521-3ea3-445a-958b-d64302191775","uuid":"fc2b8aea-5c0c-4d95-a496-24514b9206b7","timestamp":"2026-04-13T14:27:04.954Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays\n\nReplace per-AIR Round 0 kernel launches with batched descriptor-array kernels for both zerocheck constraint evaluation and logup interaction evaluation. Currently, each of the ~310 AIRs per segment at APC 300 gets 2+ individual kernel launches, buffer allocations, and H2D copies, resulting in ~1500 kernel launches per segment — nsys profiling shows 76% of Round 0 wall time (294ms) is overhead, not GPU compute. By caching the interaction DAG structure at keygen and batching all per-AIR contexts into a single H2D upload + single kernel launch (using the proven descriptor-array pattern from MLE batch kernels), we expect to reduce Round 0 from 294ms to ~100ms at APC 300, saving ~190ms from STARK excl trace.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018UtBKvct6eJvfYuLiKoLg4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JdbD9xNsb5mKTjA3kczFui","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-1700-batch-round0-caller-routing\n\nRe-attempt batched descriptor-array kernel launches for Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation, using a caller-level routing strategy that avoids modifying the existing multi-stream `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` function. The previous attempt (2026-04-13-1600) failed because adding orchestration code inside the function caused Rust optimizer interference with the multi-threaded CUDA launch path. This approach routes small AIRs to a new batched processing function from the caller, adds only a minimal filter parameter to the existing function, and keeps all batched logic in a separate module. Round 0 at APC 300 is 301ms with ~200ms estimated per-AIR overhead (kernel launch, allocation, H2D/D2H, DAG construction) across 623 AIRs — batching should reduce this to ~100-150ms.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":123808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":436},"output_tokens":72,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d386d521-3ea3-445a-958b-d64302191775","uuid":"578378c1-a875-451d-956b-c329950f3c0d"}
