{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QRaAKiKHN5pPuYVdNWHM3d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-1700-batch-round0-caller-routing\n2\t\n3\tRe-attempt batched descriptor-array kernel launches for Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation, using a caller-level routing strategy that avoids modifying the existing multi-stream `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` function. The previous attempt (2026-04-13-1600) failed because adding orchestration code inside the function caused Rust optimizer interference with the multi-threaded CUDA launch path. This approach routes small AIRs to a new batched processing function from the caller, adds only a minimal filter parameter to the existing function, and keeps all batched logic in a separate module. Round 0 at APC 300 is 301ms with ~200ms estimated per-AIR overhead (kernel launch, allocation, H2D/D2H, DAG construction) across 623 AIRs — batching should reduce this to ~100-150ms.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uw2BG9BbEwwjUh8avuNUcx","session_id":"d386d521-3ea3-445a-958b-d64302191775","uuid":"7eaf320b-9163-42ad-9910-baaa467bd4a7","timestamp":"2026-04-13T14:29:40.360Z"}
