{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XxG7waQx3xH67FhMQQGW2B","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Batch Round 0 via Caller-Level Routing\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce Round 0 evaluation time at APC 300 from 301ms to ~100-150ms by batching small AIRs' kernel launches into single descriptor-array kernels, while keeping the existing `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` function's critical multi-stream code path effectively unchanged.\n6\t\n7\tThe previous attempt (2026-04-13-1600) implemented the CUDA batched kernels and FFI but failed during Rust orchestration integration: adding routing code inside `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` changed Rust's LLVM optimizer behavior for the existing multi-threaded path, causing `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` even when the batched code was never executed.\n8\t\n9\t**Key difference in this attempt**: route from the CALLER (`prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu`), not from inside the function. Add only a minimal `skip_traces` filter parameter to the existing function. Keep all batched logic in a separate `#[inline(never)]` module.\n10\t\n11\t## Current Code Path\n12\t\n13\t### Entry point\n14\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:393` — call to `prover.sumcheck_uni_round0_polys(ctx, lambda)` from within `prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu`.\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d386d521-3ea3-445a-958b-d64302191775","uuid":"57d10513-d311-443f-a0b1-9f2c05c9ed16","timestamp":"2026-04-13T14:36:57.427Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-1700-batch-round0-caller-routing/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Batch Round 0 via Caller-Level Routing\n\n## Goal\n\nReduce Round 0 evaluation time at APC 300 from 301ms to ~100-150ms by batching small AIRs' kernel launches into single descriptor-array kernels, while keeping the existing `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` function's critical multi-stream code path effectively unchanged.\n\nThe previous attempt (2026-04-13-1600) implemented the CUDA batched kernels and FFI but failed during Rust orchestration integration: adding routing code inside `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` changed Rust's LLVM optimizer behavior for the existing multi-threaded path, causing `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` even when the batched code was never executed.\n\n**Key difference in this attempt**: route from the CALLER (`prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu`), not from inside the function. Add only a minimal `skip_traces` filter parameter to the existing function. Keep all batched logic in a separate `#[inline(never)]` module.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Entry point\n`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:393` — call to `prover.sumcheck_uni_round0_polys(ctx, lambda)` from within `prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu`.\n","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":312}}}
